@node Motivation
@chapter Motivation

As a Neovim user coming to Emacs@comma{} key chords are hard to get used to@comma{}
Vim bindings are habitual@comma{} and even @samp{evil} plus
@uref{https://github.com/emacs-evil/evil-collection, evil-collection} does not
cover every Emacs corner.

@samp{god-mode} holds Control down for you@comma{} so @samp{C-x C-f} becomes @samp{x f}. That
makes it feel like Vim's Normal mode: keys bound to commands@comma{} with
text insertion as the other mode.

The @samp{god-mode} README
@uref{https://github.com/emacsorphanage/god-mode?tab=readme-ov-file#usage-with-evil, lists ways}
of using it alongside Evil@comma{} but none give a satisfactory way to run
god-mode as a persistent Evil state.
@uref{https://github.com/gridaphobe/evil-god-state, evil-god-state}
provides a one-command god state. This package adds a persistent god
state plus one-command variants in both directions.

